# 16. Project Analytics

Group sessions by project:

```text
PROJECTS

DA-YO
██████████████  438k

Portal
████████        241k

Markitdown
████            118k
```

Show:

- Sessions
- Total tokens
- Estimated cost
- Average session duration
- Last activity

---

# 17. Daily Usage Graph

Use a very simple graph.

Example:

```text
Token Usage

500k ┤             ╭╮
400k ┤      ╭╮    ╭╯╰╮
300k ┤   ╭──╯╰╮╭──╯
200k ┤╭──╯    ╰╯
100k ┤
     └────────────────────
      Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri
```

Avoid complex axes.

The graph exists to answer:

> "Am I using more Claude than usual?"

---

# 18. Attention System

The application should notify the user only for meaningful events.

Examples:

### Permission

```text
Claude needs permission

DA-YO wants to run:
npm install

[Open Session]
```

### Usage Warning

```text
Claude usage is at 90%

You have approximately 10% remaining
```

### Session Completed

```text
Claude finished

DA-YO
42.8k tokens
12m 34s
```

### Error

```text
Claude session failed

Portal
Command exited with code 1
```

Avoid notification spam.

---

# 19. Quick Actions

Clicking a session should provide:

```text
Open Terminal
Open Project
Copy Path
View Activity
Stop Session
```

Advanced future feature:

```text
Send Message
```

Only implement this if Claude Code provides a safe and reliable integration mechanism.

---

# 20. Menu Bar States

The Menu Bar icon should communicate state.

### Idle

```text
◉ Claude
```

### Active

```text
◉ 2
```

### Warning

```text
◉ 92%
```

### Critical

```text
◉ 98%
```

### Permission

```text
◉ !
```

Do not use text that makes the Menu Bar excessively wide.

---

# 21. Data Architecture

Separate the application into layers.

```text
Claude Code
     │
     ▼
Provider Adapter
     │
     ▼
Session Discovery
     │
     ├── Process Monitor
     ├── Session Parser
     ├── Activity Parser
     ├── Token Parser
     └── Usage Parser
     │
     ▼
Normalized Domain Model
     │
     ▼
Local Storage
     │
     ▼
View Model
     │
     ├── Menu Bar
     ├── Popover
     ├── Dashboard
     └── Notifications
```

Do NOT tightly couple UI code to Claude Code's raw files/processes.

---

# 22. Provider Abstraction

Design the internal architecture so future providers can be added.

```text
AIProvider
 ├── ClaudeCodeProvider
 ├── CodexProvider
 └── GeminiCLIProvider
```

Each provider should expose normalized data:

```typescript
interface AISession {
  id: string
  provider: AIProviderType

  pid?: number

  projectName: string
  workingDirectory: string

  status: SessionStatus

  currentActivity?: string

  startedAt: Date
  lastActivityAt: Date

  usage: TokenUsage

  model?: string
}

interface TokenUsage {
  inputTokens: number
  outputTokens: number
  cacheReadTokens?: number
  cacheCreationTokens?: number

  totalTokens: number
}

interface UsageWindow {
  name: string
  usedPercent?: number
  remainingPercent?: number
  resetAt?: Date
}
```

---

# 23. Technical Direction

Preferred implementation:

## Option A — Native macOS

```text
Swift
SwiftUI
MenuBarExtra
SQLite
Foundation
OSLog
Process
FileManager
File System Events
```

Prefer this option if native macOS performance and integration are priorities.

---

## Option B — Tauri

```text
Tauri
Rust
React
TypeScript
SQLite
```

This is acceptable if rapid UI development and TypeScript are more important.

Do NOT use Electron unless there is a strong reason.

---

# 24. Performance Requirements

The application is an always-running background utility.

Target:

```text
CPU:
Near-zero when idle

Memory:
As low as reasonably possible

Startup:
< 1 second target

UI:
No noticeable lag

Polling:
Avoid aggressive polling
```

Prefer event-driven monitoring where possible.

Debounce filesystem changes.

Do not repeatedly parse entire log directories.

---

# 25. Local-First Architecture

The application should work without a backend.

Use:

```text
Local process monitoring
Local filesystem
Local SQLite
Local calculations
```

No cloud service is required for MVP.

Privacy is a core selling point:

> Your coding activity stays on your Mac.

Do not upload session content to external servers.

---

# 26. Privacy

Never collect or transmit:

- Source code
- Prompt content
- Terminal output
- File contents

unless the user explicitly enables an optional feature that requires it.

The application should only read the minimum metadata required to calculate:

- Session
- Path
- Status
- Activity
- Token usage
- Usage state

Provide a Settings section explaining what data is accessed.

---

# 27. UI Design System

The visual language should be:

```text
Minimal
Monochrome-first
Soft contrast
Rounded
Compact
Technical
Calm
Premium
```

Avoid:

```text
Huge gradients
Neon cyberpunk
Excessive cards
3D effects
Heavy shadows
Large typography
Dashboard clutter
```

Use a single accent color for state emphasis.

Use semantic states rather than decorative colors.

---

# 28. Animation

Animation should communicate state, not decorate.

Good:

```text
Energy bar slowly updating
Active session indicator pulsing gently
Usage ring animating when value changes
```

Bad:

```text
Constant particle effects
Large transitions
Bouncing cards
Excessive glow
```

Animations should respect:

```text
Reduce Motion
```

macOS accessibility preferences.

---

# 29. Accessibility

Support:

- Dynamic Type where applicable
- Keyboard navigation
- VoiceOver labels
- High contrast
- Reduce Motion
- Clear status text
- Do not rely on color alone

Example:

Do not show only:

```text
🔴
```

Show:

```text
! Permission Required
```

---

# 30. Settings

Keep settings simple.

### General

```text
Launch at Login        ON
Show Menu Bar Usage    ON
Notifications          ON
```

### Display

```text
Menu Bar Style
○ Minimal
○ Usage
○ Sessions
```

### Monitoring

```text
Refresh Interval
○ Automatic
○ 1 second
○ 5 seconds
○ 10 seconds
```

Prefer Automatic/event-driven.

### Privacy

```text
Local-only monitoring
✓ Enabled
```

---

